WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.920
Some of the most important discoveries&nbsp;
in Elden Ring's early-game..are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.520
surprisingly easy to miss. 
For example, one of the most valuable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.800
consumables in Elden Ring is the Flask of&nbsp;
Wondrous Physick, which has its single charge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.040
replenished every time you rest at a grace&nbsp;
checkpoint. That alone should easily earn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.520
it an esteemed place on your quick-select&nbsp;
bar, as it's the sort of thing you should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:26.640
try to consume for every major encounter. 
You can find your flask at the Third Church&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.200
of Marika, located to the east... here.
But what does it do? Well..that's up to you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.160
By mixing in different crystal tear combinations&nbsp;
at a grace checkpoint, you can alter its effects.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:42.080
For example, here, my crimsonburst tear heals me&nbsp;
over time, and my opaline bubbletear gives me a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.240
shield that protects me from the next attack&nbsp;
I'll be hit by. You can get both of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:51.520
tears from the field boss fought here.
Another essential item is the Whetstone Knife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.560
which allows you to apply ashes of war to your&nbsp;
armaments. You can find a Whetstone Knife here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:08.800
in a cellar underneath the Gateside Ruins. With&nbsp;
this, your weapons can get new skills..and new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:14.080
scaling options to better suit your build.
If you want to quickly get a lot of ashes of war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:28.960
make sure to visit Bernahl during the&nbsp;
day here, at the Warmaster's Shack.
&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.000
And if you find yourself wielding two weapons,&nbsp;
then you might want to duplicate an ash of war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:50.240
for both of them. To do this, you'll need to trade&nbsp;
Lost Ashes of War at the Blacksmith.
&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.240
You're going to want to talk to the blacksmith&nbsp;
pretty early, since the smithing table at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:00.400
Church of Elleh can only get your weapons to +3,&nbsp;
and the blacksmith can take them well beyond that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:05.200
To talk to him though, first, we'll have to&nbsp;
be invited to the roundtable hold. It's hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.400
to know exactly what triggers Melina to invite&nbsp;
you... I know you definitely get taken there if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.600
you defeat Margitt at Stormveil Castle ... but&nbsp;
failing that, you will eventually get invited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:24.240
simply after exploring the world for a while.
Defeating Margitt is also important because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:30.960
gives you your first Talisman Pouch. With each&nbsp;
pouch you collect, you gain another talisman slot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:39.600
Talismans are like rings from previous&nbsp;
games, offering powerful and diverse benefits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.160
to your character.
Just like talismans, your spell memorisation slots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:49.840
are now also tied to key items. So, If you want&nbsp;
to memorise more than two spells at a time, then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:55.440
you'll need to seek out Memory Stones. Your first&nbsp;
Memory Stone can be found at Iridys Rise, where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.480
you'll have to solve a simple puzzle in order&nbsp;
to gain access, and open the chest within.
&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.800
Put this in your new memory slot: the world&nbsp;
is more dangerous at night. In addition to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:12.080
night-enemies, tons of night-bosses also seem to&nbsp;
spawn. So, if you're looking for more night bosses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:21.360
you think you might have missed in the early-game,&nbsp;
head here ..... here....here.... and here. 
&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.280
To offset this apparent rise in&nbsp;
world difficulty, in my experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:35.680
your rune acquisition at night is also boosted.&nbsp;
This is thanks to three new mechanics. 
&nbsp;

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:41.840
The first, is this. When the Erdtree graces you&nbsp;
with the golden rain of its leaves, you've just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:48.560
chanced upon a rare weather effect that buffs your&nbsp;
character. What does it do? Well..I'm not sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.880
exactly. The icon here is that of a four-fingered&nbsp;
fowl foot, which has items that increase item&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.880 --> 00:04:03.680
discovery and rune aquisition. Now..the guide says&nbsp;
that the fowl foot increases rune acquisition by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:10.480
5%..so I guess that's likely to be correct,&nbsp;
though my testing revealed nothing of the sort.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:16.560
The only other option is that it boosts item&nbsp;
acquisition. Whatever the case, it's probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.920
a good idea to farm some enemies while this&nbsp;
buff is active, based on the icon, at least.
&nbsp;

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:28.240
The second thing to look out for are enemies with&nbsp;
golden eyes. In my experience, these enemies drop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:34.720
4x the amount of runes when killed. So if you&nbsp;
see an enemy with golden eyes..kill them. I love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:39.920
this mechanic. It encourages you to take up some&nbsp;
fights that you might usually have ran past. 
&nbsp;

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:45.760
Last, but not least - be on the lookout&nbsp;
for glowing white skulls upon the ground.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.720
Once broken apart, these will give you golden&nbsp;
rune consumables. They spawn in random locations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:55.600
and can be easily looted by trampling them with&nbsp;
torrent and spamming the loot button. 
&nbsp;

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.800
Some folks will want to spend these&nbsp;
runes on becoming more powerful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:05.920
but that's lame. Instead, you should spend&nbsp;
them on looking gorgeous, and getting that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:09.680
Elden Bling. (use new trailer footage)
What I'm doing here is called Armour Alteration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.880
where elements of some sets of armour can be&nbsp;
changed for a small price. For example, a cloak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.840
can be added to the commoner set, and prophets&nbsp;
can be freed from their neckpiece. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:24.640
every armour piece is different, so check it&nbsp;
out for 500 runes, and see what changes. 
&nbsp;

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:28.480
To unlock armour alteration, you'll have&nbsp;
to defeat the boss of the Demi-human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:32.400
Cave [CHECK] in southwestern Limgrave.&nbsp;
When you're victorious, you'll receive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:37.520
the tailoring kit, and a sewing needle.
The tailoring kit unlocks armour alteration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:42.400
but the sewing needle is actually a part&nbsp;
of Boc's questline. Boc's questline can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:48.240
started in a grove of trees located here ...&nbsp;
and I suspect his questline might lead towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.680
more armour alteration.
When I started this build,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:58.560
I wanted to be a glorious faithful valkyrie kind&nbsp;
of character. Then I found a black crossbow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:05.200
a spell that casts darkness, and an evil looking&nbsp;
flail. These things were way too edgy 5 me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.720
but luckily, in Elden Ring, you can&nbsp;
change your character's appearance to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:14.960
better suit your build! So that's what I did. 
It's easy to miss, but in Fia's room at Roundtable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:22.240
Hold, go up to this mirror. Here, you'll be&nbsp;
able to return to the character creation screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.520
and change everything except your&nbsp;
starting stats and keepsake.
&nbsp;

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:31.760
Make sure you frequently return to Roundtable&nbsp;
hold to see if anything's changed, or if any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:36.960
new NPC's have dropped by. Roderika should be&nbsp;
one of the first new appearances - and while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:44.960
you can first talk to her here, at the Stormhill&nbsp;
shack..that doesn't seem absolutely necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:51.840
for her questline. Progress, and she should&nbsp;
eventually show up at Roundtable hold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:58.160
whether you've talked to her before or not. 
By talking to her, then the blacksmith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:04.800
then her again, you can trigger a progression&nbsp;
in her questline. After reloading the area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:10.640
she will have found her purpose - as a spirit&nbsp;
tuner, someone who you should return to frequently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:14.640
to upgrade the strength of your favourite&nbsp;
phantoms. Of course, if you haven't already,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.600
you can get the spirit summon bell from Renna,&nbsp;
when you return to the Church of Elleh. 
&nbsp;

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:23.040
The resource used for upgrading&nbsp;
your spirits is called Glovewort.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:28.560
Regular spirits require Grave Glovewort, and&nbsp;
special spirits require Ghost Glovewort. Glovewort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:34.160
is found all throughout catacomb dungeons, and&nbsp;
unlike other resources, it doesn't appear to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:39.280
respawn after resting at a grace checkpoint, so&nbsp;
be sure to loot these dungeons thoroughly.
&nbsp;

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:45.040
Number 9 is one of my favourite new things they've&nbsp;
added to the game, bar none. Paintings. After you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:50.720
interact with one, the puzzle has begun. Your&nbsp;
job now is to go and find that place depicted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:55.200
in the painting...in the actual world. 
This painting, for example, asked me to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.960
find these gravestones. I remembered seeing&nbsp;
them a while ago, so I tracked them down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:06.640
and was rewarded by the painter. I got a scarab&nbsp;
headpiece that increases my damage taken, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:12.080
increases the damage my spells do.
The second painting was far trickier. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:17.440
was this one, in Stormveil Castle. I'm not going&nbsp;
to tell you where it depicts - but I will give you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:23.200
an important clue for all your paintings going&nbsp;
forward - remember: you don't have to find the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:28.640
place depicted in the painting. You have to&nbsp;
find the location it was painted FROM. 
&nbsp;

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:33.680
If you ever need to review the paintings you're&nbsp;
tracking, you can find them in your inventory menu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:38.480
here, at the top of the screen.
A new feature in Elden Ring are Group Passwords.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:43.920
Unlike Multiplayer Passwords, which restrict&nbsp;
you to ONLY interact with players using the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:49.520
password - Group Passwords simply let you visually&nbsp;
distinguish who is using the same password as you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:57.040
and who isn't. For example, this sign on&nbsp;
the left is using the same group password,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:02.480
and the sign on the right..isn't. The same&nbsp;
goes for phantoms, messages, and bloodstains,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:07.200
and I think it will be cool to see others from&nbsp;
our community while you're playing the game. 
&nbsp;

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:12.720
So..I want to make a community group called&nbsp;
"Secret Seekers". Our community password will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:17.360
"SEEKERS", all capitalised like that. As&nbsp;
a secret seeker, it's your job to drop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:23.040
your gold summon sign, or a message, and guide&nbsp;
others to a secret..whether that's a dungeon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:28.240
or a hidden path nearby. If you're happy with&nbsp;
a message, then upvote it! And if you have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.400
good co-op session that leads to finding&nbsp;
a new secret, then consider dropping a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:37.440
reward for your fellow seeker! Remember, our&nbsp;
community password is "SEEKERS". 
